  "scope": "Unchanged WildernessZone, DarkZone (with its DARKNESS_OVERLAY component and insect pulse), LightSource, BrawlingGloves, Event, EventHook, ZoneBuilder (startup included), MapZone, ZoneMonitor, ZoneBorders, Zone, ZoneType, ZoneRestriction, RegionZone, BankZone, KaramjaZone, ModeratorZone, MultiwayCombatZone, MusicZone, Region.java, MapDistance and Pulse on JDK 11 with Kotlin 1.8.20 and the published ConstLib 1.4.28 (Items, NPCs, Components); PulseRunner with one added import alias for its clock. Original text inserted at generation time: RandomFunction.RANDOM, random(int), random(int, int), roll and normalRandDist(max, intensity); SkullManager.DEEP_WILD_DROP_RISK_THRESHOLD; Option._P_ATTACK; QueueStrength; UseWithEvent; Event.UsedWith; the Skills ids; Entity.isTeleBlocked; and the Location, RegionManager.forId, RegionChunk.clear, Pathfinder.isStandingIn and Log texts of the zones oracle. Everything else is a recording adapter answering from the case: Entity, Player, NPC, Familiar and their sub-objects (SkullManager getters and setters, the familiar manager, appearance, interaction options, properties and combat pulse, the impact handler, extensions, event hooks, inventory and equipment snapshots, rights, username), Item names, the InterfaceManager overlay members (openOverlay, closeOverlay, close(Component) and getOverlay keep the original order of the component callbacks; the definition-type repair and packets are not modelled), Component.open/close as the base class, the skillcape perk, queueScript, stopExecuting, runTask, getItemName, GameWorld settings, GroundItemManager, Repository.sendNews and the AggressiveHandler constructor. Queued scripts and tasks run when the case says so; the insect pulse runs on the real PulseRunner. Not exercised: the real SkullManager (deep-wilderness skull icons, teleport lock), the InterfaceManager internals, the event dispatch that calls process, and dynamic regions.",
